Disable numbat's optional "plotting" (plotly) feature for numbat-cli.

plotly 0.12.1's Plot::show()/show_html()/show_image() call the private
helper Plot::show_with_default_app() unconditionally on every non-wasm
target (plotly-0.12.1/src/plot.rs:249-315, guarded only by
`#[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]`), but that helper is itself only
*defined* for `cfg(all(unix, not(target_os = "android"), not(target_os
= "macos")))` (plot.rs:550). Android is unix but excluded from the impl,
so building for any Termux/Android target (aarch64, arm, i686, x86_64)
fails with:

    error[E0599]: no associated function or constant named
    `show_with_default_app` found for struct `Plot` in the current scope

This is an upstream bug in the plotly crate itself (the caller-side cfg
doesn't match the definition-side cfg for Android), not something numbat
can be expected to work around, and "opening a plot in the OS's default
viewer app" doesn't make sense in a Termux terminal session anyway.
Disable numbat's "plotting" feature (default-features = false, keep only
fetch-exchangerates) so plotly is never compiled in, while still shipping
currency-conversion support.

--- a/numbat-cli/Cargo.toml
+++ b/numbat-cli/Cargo.toml
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 anyhow = "1"
 rustyline = { version = "16.0.0", features = ["derive"] }
 dirs = "6"
-numbat = { version = "1.24.0", path = "../numbat" }
+numbat = { version = "1.24.0", path = "../numbat", default-features = false, features = ["fetch-exchangerates"] }
 colored = "3"
 itertools = "0.14"
 toml = { version = "0.8.8", features = ["parse"] }
